# the run time has nothing to enter for a member of %CompilerHelpers% whose row names a function of the compiler, so the call has no closed form by value: it is a direct call of that function, whatever is withheld
# function inTailPosition(x) { return createElement(x, "t"); }
# RUN: walk f4 mechanisms=none
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK: [[call]]: {{*}} = CallDirect {{*}}function=f1
# CHECK: ReturnCall [[call]]
# RUN(NEVER): walk f4 mechanisms=none
# NEVER-NOT: = Call v
# RUN(ALL): walk f4
# ALL-NOT: = Call v
# No summary shows who calls the function, and the host never does: it has code because that code names it.
# RUN(REACHED): units-with-code f1 f2 f3 mechanisms=none
# REACHED: unit f1:Body {{*}} bytes
# REACHED: unit f2:Body {{*}} bytes
# REACHED: unit f3:Body {{*}} bytes
# PROGRAM-OF: ../../answers/built-in-without-a-function-object-enters-the-function-of-its-row.ir
